{"id":"u-e1017acb-4302-46dd-8346-4496fa228628","src":"community","title":"Pocock Strength & Mass: The Hypertrophy (Part 2)","author":"Kevin A","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/cXAoGq-pocock-strength-and-mass-the-hypertrophy-part-2","desc":"Welcome to Part 2 of the David Pocock rugby training series. After building an explosive foundation in the Strength-Power block and taking a recovery week, it’s time to shift focus. The explicit purpose of this next phase is to pack on lean muscle mass and build structural size, utilizing the exact hypertrophy principles that prepare elite rugby union athletes for the physical demands of international competition.\n\nKey Elements of this Hypertrophy Phase:\n\nHigh Training Volume: Step up the workload with increased sets and reps designed to push your limits.\n\nTargeted Muscle Damage: Stimulate deep muscular growth and adaptation through progressive, high-intensity volume.\n\nCritical Nutrition Support: Because of the intense physical demands of this block, ensuring your diet includes enough high-quality protein for muscle growth and repair is absolutely essential to seeing results.\n\nPush through the volume, nail your recovery, and build the dense, functional muscle mass needed to dominate.\n\nWhat's Next:\nOnce you complete this block, take a week off to fully recover, retest your 1RM (One-Rep Maxes), and start Part 1 (Strength-Power) again with your new, updated strength baselines.\n\n🔥 Coming Soon: Part 3 (Pure Strength)\nDesigned specifically for athletes who need to maximize raw, absolute strength.\n\nKey components of this upcoming phase:\n\nThorough Warm-Up Sets: Preparing your nervous system and joints for heavy loads.\n\nMaximal Effort Work Sets: High-intensity efforts to force neuromuscular adaptation.\n\nAdequate Recovery Between Work Sets: Crucial rest intervals to ensure high-quality output on every single set.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength","